cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "hpotential: reproducible code for the H-potential health-capability methods series"
abstract: >-
  Code behind six manuscripts on health capability: a second-order measurement
  model and the structural ceiling on its factor-score determinacy, a two-stage
  prognostic pipeline, a modified Delphi consensus rule and its error rates, a
  continuous-time state model with verified solvers, a costed access-versus-
  efficacy rule, and an early health technology assessment with value of
  information. All data are synthetic.
type: software
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-15"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Nube1/h-potential-companions"
authors:
  - name: "H-potential methods series authors"
keywords:
  - psychometrics
  - factor score determinacy
  - item response theory
  - Delphi
  - differential item functioning
  - health technology assessment
  - value of information
